 "headline": "",
 "intro": "SUNDANCE TOOK THEIR FESTIVAL COMPLETELY VIRTUAL in 2022, TASKING IHC To ATTRACT YOUNG AUDIENCEs TO TAP IN AND JOIN THE ONLINE CONVERSATION.",
 "introPieces": [
  {
   "type": "introGallery",
   "media": [
    {
     "type": "image",
     "src": "/images/6a5148d7d715577e5b7b2d16_sundance.avif",
     "alt": ""
    }
   ],
   "html": "<p>IHC developed a social strategy around the theme of Convergence. Working with a last minute change to going fully virtual, we executed an exciting digital campaign that produced boundary-pushing content and drove digital dialogue among all audiences that made 2022's festival one to remember.</p>\n<p>To do this, we focused on two major platforms, Twitter, where we took over all interactivity, and TikTok, launching Sundance for the first time.</p>"
  }
 ],
 "sections": [
  {
   "title": "TIKTOK Strategy",
   "pieces": [
    {
     "type": "text2",
     "left": "<p>We sought to convert the next generation of film fans onto the #Sundance experience through creating original, talent-centric content. 10 verticals were developed to introduce the festival to TikTok, highlight special events and can’t miss moments, and introduce fans to the virtual festival format.</p>",
     "right": "<p>IHC brought unique content themes &amp; scripts for each video that established a unique tone of voice. Creators like Reggie Watts, Ella Watkins, JD Samson, Isaac Hinden-Miller, and Illeleana were paired with specific themes to create content and generate community engagement. </p>"
    },
